			"Message": "docs(Deps): Add two-step build instructions for VS Code source compilation\n\nUpdate the README.md within the Dependency submodule to clarify the build workflow. Explicitly define the two-step linear flow: first compiling the VS Code source in `Dependency/Microsoft/Dependency/Editor` using Node 22 and the `dum` tooling, then building the Land application from the root.\n\nInclude critical warnings against recursive submodule cloning, emphasizing that each dependency is managed independently on its own branch. This ensures developers avoid state corruption when synchronizing upstream patches.\n\nRefs: CodeEditorLand/Land",
			"SHA": "9260645cc729d77cacfe302923b5a34a7f1a906a"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-13T22:47:35Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				171,
				1
			],
			"Message": "sync(Deps/Editor): Update to 900a349 with Phase 9 agent host crash recovery\n\nUpdate the VS Code Editor dependency submodule from 4878f46 to 355ae1cc (upstream 900a349). This synchronization integrates critical stability improvements for the Agent Host lifecycle and terminal management, which are essential for the Cocoon extension host and Mountain backend operations.\n\nKey upstream changes include:\n- **Agent Host Phase 9:** Implemented runtime mutation for live Claude sessions, including abort, model hot-swapping, and steering. Added crash recovery mechanisms that prevent permanent fatal latches, enabling robust subprocess restarts and state replay.\n- **Terminal Reliability:** Fixed background terminal accumulation issues and enforced strict trust checks for local terminals within remote workspaces.\n- **Bug Fixes:** Resolved null guard issues in configuration trees, corrected off-by-one errors in extension pagination, and fixed protected modifier visibility.\n- **UI Enhancements:** Enabled output renderers for chat code blocks and improved markdown frontmatter rendering.\n\nThis update ensures the editor maintains stability during complex agent operations and prevents indefinite hangs or UI corruption during extension lifecycle events.\n\nRefs: microsoft/vscode",
			"SHA": "c4e9148914a3217c74ae74b29badc80c2a330caf"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-13T21:53:49Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				171,
				1
			],
			"Message": "sync(Deps/Editor): Update to 6e18ef9e with Agent Host crash recovery\n\nUpdate the VS Code Editor dependency submodule from 9ef8f21 to 4878f46. This synchronization integrates critical stability improvements for the Agent Host lifecycle and terminal management, which are essential for the Cocoon extension host and Mountain backend operations.\n\nKey upstream changes include:\n- **Agent Host Phase 9:** Implemented crash recovery mechanisms that prevent permanent fatal latches, enabling robust subprocess restarts during live Claude sessions. Added support for abort, steering, and model hot-swapping.\n- **Terminal Reliability:** Fixed background terminal accumulation issues and enforced trust checks for local terminals within remote workspaces.\n- **Bug Fixes:** Resolved null guard issues in configuration trees, corrected off-by-one errors in extension pagination, and fixed protected modifier visibility in test helpers.\n- **UI Enhancements:** Enabled output renderers for chat code blocks and improved markdown frontmatter rendering.\n\nThis update ensures the editor maintains stability during complex agent operations and prevents indefinite hangs or UI corruption during extension lifecycle events.\n\nRefs: microsoft/vscode",
			"SHA": "2dd3e155ed669fbd6c54f5e347f57bf8fd41a577"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-13T21:12:43Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				171,
				1
			],
			"Message": "sync(Deps/Editor): Update to 9ef8f21 with WKWebView ready-state fix\n\nUpdate the VS Code Editor dependency submodule from e94b4c4 to 9ef8f21. This sync addresses a critical initialization hang encountered when rendering the editor UI within the native Tauri webview on macOS.\n\nKey upstream changes included:\n- **Webview Ready-State Reliability:** Removed strict `allowScripts` dependency and specific `location.pathname` validation for `fake.html` that caused false negatives in WKWebView environments.\n- **Loading Signal Enhancement:** Added support for `readyState === 'complete'` as a valid signal for frame loading.\n\nThis update ensures stable initialization of the Sky editor UI layer when running under the Mountain native backend.",
			"SHA": "913878b98389bc0da1ffaa82ed3557659ffb1fb1"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-13T15:52:31Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				171,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Deps/Editor): Sync upstream to e94b4c4 with Agents window and SSH fixes\n\nUpdate the VS Code dependency submodule from 7c59d89 to e94b4c4. This sync incorporates significant stability improvements and feature enhancements for the Agents window and remote session management.\n\nKey upstream changes included:\n- **Agents Window Stability:** Fixed terminal lifecycle issues where hidden tool terminals were incorrectly disposed, causing chat agent tool pipeline errors. Resolved layout state persistence across reloads and corrected sticky header backgrounds.\n- **SSH & Remote Reliability:** Implemented keyboard-interactive authentication fallback for SSH hosts requiring 2FA. Added a watchdog mechanism to detect and recover from silently-dead TCP transports (half-open connections) after network changes or sleep, preventing indefinite hangs.\n- **Session Navigation:** Enhanced back/forward history to track active chat changes within sessions and restored layout state per session.\n- **Tooling & API:** Fixed `apply_patch` rendering as file edits, corrected terminal disposal ordering to prevent xterm addon errors, and enabled bracketed paste mode for agent host terminals.\n- **Configuration:** Renamed `extensions.supportSessionsWindow` to `extensions.supportAgentsWindow`.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: The setting `extensions.supportSessionsWindow` has been renamed to `extensions.supportAgentsWindow`.\nRefs: microsoft/vscode#315523",
			"SHA": "efa3b8d9924e509a58d5515c2b3c6491f29b409b"
		}
	],
